module fixture.closure.rustc_empty_map_data_turbofish_probe

import std.types { String }

// map_insert IS IMPORTED AND empty_map IS DELIBERATELY NOT. That asymmetry is the fixture: the
// defect needs v2.std.collection in the closure, because that is where the `empty_map<K, V>() ->
// Map<K, V>` DECLARATION lives and resolving the call to it is what hands the emitter the
// declaration's own formals as the resolved return type. A module that imports empty_map, or one
// whose closure does not reach that module at all, resolves to something concrete and never carries
// the shape -- measured: with no import of this module the emission was already
// `rc_empty_map::<String, String>()`. extdeps.rust.cargo_build, where this was found, imports
// neither and reaches the module transitively; this import reproduces that reach at one symbol.
import v2.std.collection { map_insert }

// THE EMPTY-MAP TURBOFISH, POSED TO RUSTC RATHER THAN TO A SUBSTRING ORACLE. The subject is
// v1.compiler.emit_rust rust_empty_map_init_expr: a `Map<K, V>` literal built by empty_map() must be
// instantiated from the type the author declared, and where the resolved return type arrived as the
// Map DECLARATION's own parametric shape -- which is what this module gets, because it resolves Map
// by namespace alone rather than importing it -- the key and value types must be deferred to the
// target's own inference. Before that decision the emission wrote the declaration's formals
// straight out, producing `v1_rt::rc_empty_map::<K, V>()` inside a non-generic module: rustc E0425,
// `cannot find type K in this scope`. Measured on extdeps.rust.cargo_build cargo_compile_env, which
// is this exact shape.
//
// WHY A SPELLING ORACLE CANNOT BE THE SUBJECT HERE. The defective and the repaired emissions differ
// only in the two identifiers inside one turbofish, and asserting the PRESENCE of either `String,
// String` or `_, _` pins one of two renderings that are both correct depending on whether the map
// type resolved concretely. What has to hold is that the emitted turbofish NAMES SOMETHING THAT
// EXISTS at the point it is written, which is a scoping question and therefore rustc's.
//
// THE THREE DECLARATIONS ARE THREE POSITIONS, NOT VARIETY. A module-scope `data` initializer has no
// enclosing generic scope at all, so a formal written there can never bind; a non-generic fn body is
// the same loss one level in; and the fold accumulator is the position that already carried this
// repair, kept here as the arm that must not regress while the other two are fixed beside it.
data module_scope_env: Map<String, String> = empty_map()

fn fn_body_env() -> Map<String, String> {
  empty_map()
}

fn folded_env(keys: List<String>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(keys, init: empty_map(), f: (acc, k) => map_insert(acc, k, k))
}

fn env_word_count(keys: List<String>) -> Int {
  count(map_keys(module_scope_env)) + count(map_keys(fn_body_env())) + count(map_keys(folded_env(keys: keys)))
}
